[38;2;124;124;124mNow the proof is cleaner:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. I is prime (verified by primary decomposition: I = √I, single component).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. ht(I) = 3, so dim(R/I) = 3.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. The minimal free resolution of R/I over R has length 3 (Betti numbers 1, 6, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m8, 3), so pd_R(R/I) = 3 = ht(I).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m4. By Auslander-Buchsbaum (R is regular, hence CM, with depth(R) = 6): depth(R/[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mI) = depth(R) - pd(R/I) = 6 - 3 = 3 = dim(R/I).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m5. Therefore R/I is Cohen-Macaulay of dimension 3.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, I should present this as a proof. The computational parts (primary [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdecomposition, Gröbner basis resolution) are the key verifications. Let me also [0m[38;2;124;124;124mexhibit the regular sequence explicitly and verify the Hilbert series [0m
